---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **어느 달에 가장 많이 읽히나.** (`/peak-month`)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 ────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 774팀의 «봉우리달»을 이미 갖고 있었다(9/07 group-afterlife). 그런데 그 자료로
 * 「봉우리 뒤 얼마나 남나」만 물었고, **「봉우리가 어느 달에 오나」는 안 물었다.**
 * 우물을 다시 길어 오지 않고 있는 자료를 다시 센 것이다 —
 * 사장님: 「우리는 raw data 를 가공하는 회사다」.
 *
 * ── 🔴 이 지면이 반드시 보이는 보정 ─────────────────────────────
 * 2월은 28일이라 열람이 덜 쌓이고, 그러면 그 달이 봉우리가 될 확률도 낮다.
 * 그냥 12로 나눈 기대치에 대면 2월이 «저절로» 낮게 나온다.
 * ⭐ 그래서 창 안에 실제로 든 날수로 기대치를 만들었고, **표에 그 날수를 함께 낸다.**
 *   보정을 안 보여 주면 손님이 우리 셈을 검산할 수 없다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 하지 않는 것 ─────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 「1월에 컴백하면 잘 된다」로 읽히게 쓰지 않는다. 컴백 달은 우리 자료에 없다
 * ⛔ 「읽힌 것」을 「인기」로 바꿔 쓰지 않는다
 * ⛔ 작은 표본에 표준편차를 붙이지 않는다 — 자가 서른 미만이면 안 낸다
 *
 * ── 새 지면을 낼 때 밟는 넷 (2026-09-07 에 셋을 빠뜨렸다) ───────────
 *   1. src/pages/wikitip/sitemap.xml.ts 목록      ✅ 같은 커밋에서 넣었다
 *   2. canonical=  (⛔ page= 가 아니다 — 레이아웃이 조용히 버린다)  ✅
 *   3. jsonLd — Dataset 스키마                    ✅
 *   4. KcwRelatedArticles — 기사로 가는 문         ✅
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/kcw-peak-month.json';

const 전체 = d.전체;
const 큰 = d.큰팀;
const 줄 = 전체.줄;
const 높은순 = [...줄].filter((x) => x.표준편차 !== null).sort((a, b) => b.표준편차 - a.표준편차);
const 으뜸 = 높은순[0];
const 꼴찌 = 높은순[높은순.length - 1];
const 빈달 = 큰.줄.filter((x) => x.팀수 === 0);

const TITLE = `${으뜸.이름} is when a K-pop act is read most. ${꼴찌.이름} is when it is not`;
const DESC =
  `We found the single best-read month of ${전체.잰팀} Korean acts on English Wikipedia. `
  + `${으뜸.팀수} of them peaked in ${으뜸.이름}, ${꼴찌.팀수} in ${꼴찌.이름} — against an `
  + `expectation corrected for how many days each month contributes.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: d.창,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/', 'https://query.wikidata.org/'],
};

const 수 = (n) => (n == null ? '—' : Number(n).toLocaleString('en-US'));
/* 표에서 눈에 걸리게 — 두 표준편차를 넘은 것만 굵게 */
const 뚜렷 = (z) => z !== null && Math.abs(z) >= 2;
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/peak-month">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Every Korean act has one month when more people looked it up on English Wikipedia than in
    any other. We know that month for <b>{수(전체.잰팀)} acts</b>. Sorted by calendar month,
    they are not spread evenly: <b>{으뜸.팀수}</b> peaked in {으뜸.이름} and only
    {' '}<b>{꼴찌.팀수}</b> in {꼴찌.이름}.
  </p>

  {/* 🔴 [2026-09-07] 처음엔 잰 팀 수를 «본문에만» 적었다. 표 약속 검사가 잡았다 —
      「본문 문장에 스친 수는 표가 아니다」. 옳은 지적이라 표를 냈고, 손님에게도
      「무엇을 셌나」가 한눈에 보이는 칸이 생겼다. 자를 글에 맞추지 않고 글을 자에 맞춘다. */}
  <section class="src">
    <h2>What was counted</h2>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Korean acts whose best-read month we know</td><td class="num"><b>{수(전체.잰팀)}</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Acts dropped for too few months — <i>not counted as zero</i></td><td class="num">{수(전체.못잰팀)}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Of those, peaks of {수(큰.문턱)} reads or more</td><td class="num">{수(큰.잰팀)}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Months in the window</td><td class="num">{수(줄.reduce((a, b) => a + b.창안날수, 0))} days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Calendar months more than two SD from expectation</td><td class="num"><b>{줄.filter((x) => 뚜렷(x.표준편차)).length}</b> of 12</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Why this needs a correction before you read it</h2>
    <p class="note">
      February has 28 days. A short month collects fewer reads, so it is <i>less likely</i> to
      hold an act's best month for reasons that have nothing to do with music. Our window also
      starts in July, so July and August appear one more time than the other months. Both
      effects are corrected below, and the day counts are printed so you can check the
      arithmetic. Without the correction February would read as 59% of expectation; with it,
      {' '}{줄[1].기대대비몫}%.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>The month each act was read most, all {수(전체.잰팀)} of them</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <caption>
          Expectation is proportional to the days each calendar month contributes to
          {' '}{d.창}. Standard deviations are shown only because the sample passes 30 acts.
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Month</th><th class="num">Acts</th><th class="num">Days in window</th>
            <th class="num">Expected</th><th class="num">Of expected</th><th class="num">SD</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {줄.map((x) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{x.이름}</td>
              <td class="num">{뚜렷(x.표준편차) ? <b>{x.팀수}</b> : x.팀수}</td>
              <td class="num fine">{수(x.창안날수)}</td>
              <td class="num fine">{x.기대치}</td>
              <td class="num">{x.기대대비몫 == null ? '—' : `${x.기대대비몫}%`}</td>
              <td class="num">{x.표준편차 == null ? '—' : x.표준편차}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Three months sit more than two standard deviations from expectation on the high side or
      the low side. That is the finding. The middle of the table is unremarkable, and we say so
      rather than dressing it up.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>The 100 biggest peaks, and the month that never wins</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Restricted to the {수(큰.잰팀)} acts whose best month drew at least
      {' '}{수(큰.문턱)} reads, so that a small article having a noisy month cannot drive the
      pattern.
      {빈달.length === 1 && (
        <>
          {' '}Among those hundred, <b>not one</b> peaked in {빈달[0].이름} — against an
          expectation of {빈달[0].기대치}.
        </>
      )}
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Month</th><th class="num">Acts</th><th class="num">Expected</th><th class="num">SD</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {큰.줄.map((x) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{x.이름}</td>
              <td class="num">{x.팀수 === 0 ? <b>0</b> : x.팀수}</td>
              <td class="num fine">{x.기대치}</td>
              <td class="num">{x.표준편차 == null ? '—' : x.표준편차}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      The pattern is weaker here than in the full set. Whatever produces it works mostly on
      acts that are read in the thousands, not the hundreds of thousands — and that is worth
      saying plainly, because the opposite would have been the more quotable result.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    {d.이것이아닌것.map((l) => <p class="note">{l}</p>)}
    <p class="note">
      In particular: we do not hold release dates. If you want to read this as “release in
      {' '}{으뜸.이름}”, that is a different claim about data we did not collect.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where else this leads</h2>
    <p class="note">
      The same {수(전체.잰팀)} acts lose half of that peak within
      {' '}<a href="/group-afterlife">two months of reaching it</a>, and the median act takes
      two years after debut to get there. Korean <i>titles</i>
      {' '}<a href="/half-life">halve on the same two-month timescale</a>. Birthdays run on a
      different calendar again — <a href="/kpop-birthdays">July is the thinnest month</a> for
      K-pop birthdays, which is not the month that shows up here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/peak-month" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <p class="note">
      {d.우물} Window {d.창}; the current month is excluded because it is unfinished.
      Re-counted {d.잰때}.
    </p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
  .src { margin: 1.6rem 0; }
  .src h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: .92rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: .5rem 0; }
  .scroll-x { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .92rem; }
  caption { text-align: left; color: var(--muted); font-size: .86rem;
    line-height: 1.55; padding-bottom: .5rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: .4rem .5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  th.num, td.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .fine { color: var(--muted); font-size: .86rem; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { table { font-size: .88rem; } h1 { font-size: 1.35rem; } }
</style>
